# Walkthrough - Database Reset and Seeding (v5)

## Changes
The database has been reset and seeded using the **corrected Sonatrach hierarchy**, an **extended timeframe**, **Custom Emission Factors**, and **Mitigation Actions**.
- Verified [manage-data.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/manage-data.html) successfully fetches and displays mitigation records via `/api/mitigation`.
- Confirmed [dashboard.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/dashboard.js) integrates mitigation data into "Net Emissions" and "GHG Mitigation" using the API response.
- **Implemented Missing UI**: Added `/api/factors` to [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/server.js) and updated [reference-data.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/reference-data.html) to fetch and display custom emission factors dynamically.
    - Custom factors seeded with [seed_sonatrach_full.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/seed_sonatrach_full.js) are now visible in the "Reference Data" page under a "Custom & Regional Factors" category.
    - Verified [manage-data.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/manage-data.html) also utilizes the new `/api/factors` endpoint for managing custom factors.
- **Enhanced Production Data Filters**:
    - Replaced the static year input with a dynamic dropdown in [manage-data.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/manage-data.html).
    - Added `/api/production/years` to [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/server.js) to fetch distinct years from the database.
    - Updated `/api/production` to support an 'all' years filter.
    - **Debugging**: Resolved an issue where filtered data was not appearing by removing redundant logic in [server.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/server.js) and restarting the server.
    - **Frontend Fix**: Corrected [manage-data.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/manage-data.html) to ensure "All Years" is selected by default, preventing the dropdown from auto-selecting 2024.
    - **Crash Fix**: Removed undefined function calls (`loadScope3`, `loadEFactors`) that were preventing the page from initializing correctly.
    - **Intensity Dashboard**: Updated [carbon-intensity.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/carbon-intensity.js) to dynamically load years from the database, fixing the issue where only partial years were visible.

